## No third-party responses are redistributed here

This is the simple case, and it is worth stating plainly: **this package ships
no item responses at all.**

The simulation evidence — the Phase 14 pilot, the Phase 15 training and
held-out validation tiers, and the Phase 16 fresh confirmation with its 86,400
raw replication rows — is synthetic, generated from the documented seed tree in
[`provenance/seed-tree.md`](provenance/seed-tree.md). It carries no upstream
terms.

The application evidence — the twelve Phase 17 draw streams under
`data-frozen/empirical/aws-raw/`, 99,999 draws each — consists of bootstrap
draws of the scalability coefficient. It is derived from `SWMDK` but contains
no respondent-level data.

## Where the application data comes from

`SWMDK` is distributed inside the **`mokken`** R package, which is why `mokken`
is a *required* dependency of this package rather than an optional one. Load it
with `data(SWMDK)`; the pipeline consumed it read-only under a locked digest,
which `verification/` asserts against your copy.

Its provenance, none of which this package can relicense:

- a documented subset of the Dutch **COOL^5-18^** cohort study;
- items from Peetsma and Van der Veen;
- subset construction following Koopman et al. (2022).

See [`DATA_ACCESS.md`](DATA_ACCESS.md) for the exact call, the locked digest,
and the version boundary.

